                <pb facs="0834" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg740"/>

                <head>No. 481.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 14, 1887</date>.
                        (Received July 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg leave to call your attention to my
                    No. 76, of February 28 last, inclosing Mr. Mariscal’s note to me of the 25th,
                    offering to return certain property which had been delivered to the authorities
                    of the State of Chihuahua by United States Army officers, and also to pay $500,
                    the estimated value of other property also delivered to the same authorities,
                    and which had been lost. In his note Mr. Mariscal requests that some person be
                    appointed by the United States Government to receive the property and the
                    money.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. C. Manning.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
